From: cvediver <cvediver@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: wait for PCIe link before recovery BAR access

After an RDDM firmware crash the QCN9274's PCIe link retrains while
the group recovery path is already calling ath12k_pci_power_up(),
whose first action (ath12k_pci_sw_reset) performs BAR reads. On PC
class hosts a memory-space read to a link-down endpoint returns ~0;
on the IPQ5332 the NoC raises an Asynchronous SError (fatal machine
check), so a radio crash panics the whole system. Observed twice on a
GL.iNet GL-BE9300 via simulate_fw_crash, both panic traces ending in
ath12k_pci_read32 (once under the coredump upload, once directly
under ath12k_pci_power_up), captured by ramoops.

Poll device presence via config space (RC-terminated, safe on a down
link) with a bounded wait before the first BAR access in power_up.
On timeout, fail power-up cleanly: the WSI group recovery retry
either brings the device back on the next pass or leaves the radios
down with the system alive.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -1430,12 +1430,38 @@
 	queue_work(ab->workqueue, &ab->dump_work);
 }
 #endif
 
+static int ath12k_pci_wait_device_present(struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci)
+{
+	struct pci_dev *pdev = ab_pci->pdev;
+	struct ath12k_base *ab = ab_pci->ab;
+	int i;
+
+	/* 100 * 20 ms: post-RDDM link retrain is typically well under
+	 * a second; cold probe passes on the first iteration.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
+		if (pci_device_is_present(pdev))
+			return 0;
+		msleep(20);
+	}
+
+	ath12k_err(ab, "PCIe device absent after reset, aborting power-up\n");
+	return -ENODEV;
+}
+
 int ath12k_pci_power_up(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
 	struct ath12k_pci *ab_pci = ath12k_pci_priv(ab);
 	int ret;
 
+	/* The BAR accesses below SError on the IPQ5332 NoC if the
+	 * endpoint's link is still retraining after an RDDM crash.
+	 */
+	ret = ath12k_pci_wait_device_present(ab_pci);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	ab_pci->register_window = 0;
 	clear_bit(ATH12K_PCI_FLAG_INIT_DONE, &ab_pci->flags);
 	ath12k_pci_sw_reset(ab_pci->ab, true);
